// PLACEHOLDER — do not use as-is.
//
// FCM push requires a real Firebase config. Steps:
//   1. Create a Firebase project (console.firebase.google.com).
//   2. Add an Android app with package name  com.studybuddy.app
//   3. Download the generated google-services.json.
//   4. Save it as  apps/mobile/google-services.json  (it is gitignored).
//      For EAS builds, upload it as an EAS secret file and point
//      GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON at it.
//   5. In Expo: the Expo push service delivers to Android via FCM using this file.
//
// The real file looks like:
// {
//   "project_info": { "project_id": "...", "project_number": "...", ... },
//   "client": [ { "client_info": { "android_client_info": { "package_name": "com.studybuddy.app" } }, ... } ]
// }
